## Quality gate references

- [QG-M2 — Tenant Isolation (v1.1.0)](../../_bmad/bbp/bmad-bam-agent-atlas/resources/checklists/QG-M2.md) — `test-catalogue.json` feeds:
  - C1 (universal isolation check) — sourced from `coverage_report.isolation.must_have ≥ 1` AND ≥1 entry with `category: isolation` AND `universal: true`
  - C5 (rls-bypass coverage) — sourced from `coverage_report.rls-bypass.must_have ≥ 1` when tenancy includes row-level-security mechanism
  - H1 (test-catalogue coverage of mechanism-specific bypass) — sourced from per-mechanism bypass test count

## BMM overlay consumers

This catalogue is consumed by BMM's `bmad-qa-generate-e2e-tests` skill via the BAM customize-template overlay shipped under `bmad-bam-design-multi-tenant-testing/customize-template/bmad-qa-generate-e2e-tests/customize.toml`. The overlay's `activation_steps_append` instructs the BMM skill to:

1. Read `test-catalogue.json` at `_bmad/bam/evidence/QG-M2/`
2. Cover all `universal: true` tests as a baseline regardless of project's `tenancy_model`
3. Cover per-model tests selected by `tenancy_model` (or per-tier mechanisms in `hybrid_resolution`)
4. Treat `rls-bypass` tests as MANDATORY when any mechanism in scope == `row-level-security`

## Next steps

After this catalogue is approved:

1. Run downstream test code generation (BMM `bmad-qa-generate-e2e-tests` with the overlay applied at install time) — produces the actual test files in your repo.
2. Wire the test catalogue's `tests[].id` set into CI as the must-have gate for QG-M2 sign-off.
3. Run `bmad-bam-design-tenant-migration-tooling` if migration is in-scope; the migration runbook may pull catalogue tests as smoke-coverage for cohort dry-runs.
